WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.390
Foundations. Three parts.

2
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.420
What is the Azure SPI machinery made of?

3
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:19.460
Three parts. The Azure stack, an
environment that runs the OSDU services.

4
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.090
The service interface inside each service,

5
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.100
with the Azure provider behind it.

6
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.250
And the engineering system:

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.940
the shared workflows that keep
every service fork current.

8
00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:33.936
SPI means all three.

9
00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:37.376
The Azure stack lives
in your subscription,

10
00:00:37.406 --> 00:00:40.016
and osdu-spi-stack builds it.

11
00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:43.536
The service interface
lives in each service:

12
00:00:43.606 --> 00:00:47.296
shared OSDU code calls a
cloud provider through it,

13
00:00:47.526 --> 00:00:50.166
and the Azure implementation
sits behind it,

14
00:00:50.166 --> 00:00:51.616
in the service's fork.

15
00:00:51.846 --> 00:00:56.086
The engineering system lives
in GitHub, in osdu-spi,

16
00:00:56.086 --> 00:00:58.976
the template every fork
takes its workflows from.

17
00:01:01.076 --> 00:01:02.206
They turn together.

18
00:01:02.516 --> 00:01:05.646
A change to a provider is
made in its service's fork.

19
00:01:05.956 --> 00:01:08.686
The engineering system
builds it into an image.

20
00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:13.516
And the stack runs that image, with the
provider inside it reaching the Azure

21
00:01:13.516 --> 00:01:14.846
services around it.

22
00:01:17.312 --> 00:01:20.112
So now you can ask
which SPI someone means:

23
00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:25.002
the Azure stack, the service
interface, or the engineering system.

24
00:01:27.368 --> 00:01:30.898
Next: what is actually running
when someone says “the stack”?

